{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-q-exp-p-adic","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:q-exp-p-adic","kind":"remark","title":"$p$-adic realisations of $\\exp_q$ ($\\mathbb{Q}_p$ and $\\mathbb{C}_p$)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-q-exp-finite-field-obstruction"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-exponential","tags":["q-exponential","p-adic","witt-vectors","c-p","convergence"],"text":"q-exp-p-adic.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:q-exp-p-adic\"></a><p>The truncated <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{F}_p</code>-exponential lifts to a convergent grouplike on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Q}_p</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{C}_p</code> when <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>-adically close to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code>. For <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\in 1 + p\\mathbb{Z}_p</code>, the Jackson factorial satisfies <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">v_p([n]_q!) = v_p(n!)</code>. Over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{C}_p</code>, the series converges for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">v_p(x) > 1/(p - 1)</code>, exactly matching the classical <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>-adic exponential radius.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exp-p-adic.md","heading":"Remark","number":"3.22.6"}
